WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.167
 JON ALPERT:<i> Do you want
 to introduce me, Robert?</i>

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:03.670
-This my girl, Deliris.
-Hi.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.104
JON: What are you guys gonna do?

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:06.406
ROBERT STEFFEY:<i> Load up.</i>

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:07.439
♪ (ROCK MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

00:00:07.539 --> 00:00:09.108
Is it gonna be hard
to sell this stuff?

00:00:09.241 --> 00:00:10.243
ROBERT: No, not at all.

00:00:11.043 --> 00:00:12.779
Beats the minimum wage. (LAUGHS)

00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:15.148
It's taking a chance out here.

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:17.751
♪ (DISTORTED "HAPPY BIRTHDAY"
PLAYS) ♪

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:20.152
SPEAKER:<i> You got a pocket
full of money. You want a taste?</i>

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:21.854
JON:<i> Is your mother
 doing drugs every day?</i>

00:00:21.954 --> 00:00:22.789
(MUMBLING)

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:23.956
-(SNORTS)
-(LAUGHS)

00:00:24.623 --> 00:00:26.559
ROBERT:<i> These take
all the problems off the mind.</i>

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:29.963
♪ (PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.130
(CHUCKLES)

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.801
FREDDIE RODRIGUEZ:
<i>Our mother and father got
divorced when we were young,</i>

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.269
<i> put me in a foster home.</i>

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.671
<i>If I would've stayed there
 with those rich folks,</i>

00:00:38.771 --> 00:00:40.140
<i>I wouldn't be here right now.</i>

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:43.910
<i> We're going to find out
the results of my HIV test.</i>

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:49.015
My father works, 80 dollars
a week, for peanuts.

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:50.683
JON: You know what
your son does to make money?

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.084
ROBERT'S FATHER:
<i>Yep. I don't like the idea.</i>

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:53.186
(SIRENS WAIL)

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:56.823
ROBERT:
<i>What'd I do to get locked up?
 Dealing, doing drugs.</i>

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:58.458
<i> Free again.</i>

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:00.526
You got any jobs? I need a job.

00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:03.796
<i>A lot of people went through
a lot of trouble to help me.</i>

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.598
Now, why am I
gonna mess that up?

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:09.034
DELIRIS VASQUEZ:<i> In and out
of jail, in and out of jail.</i>

00:01:09.301 --> 00:01:11.738
If you go back on drugs,
we can't live with you.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:13.372
JON: How long you been
working the streets?

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:14.306
(TRUCK HONKS)

00:01:14.473 --> 00:01:15.508
TRUCK DRIVER: I'm waitin'.

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:19.079
DELIRIS' CHILD:
<i>If you love us so much, why
you not doing so good for us?</i>

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:20.980
You never try.

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:24.450
I don't know
what I'm gonna do with my life.

00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:26.486
DELIRIS:<i> Stay strong, okay?</i>

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:30.723
<i> Just don't give up.
 Don't give up.</i>

00:01:30.789 --> 00:01:32.191
DELIRIS' CHILD:
I know you can do it, ma.

00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:33.593 line:0%
♪ (MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

